# openJournal facts — atomic behavioral spec (MVP, integration/spec-1-mvp @ 54faa3a)

## Trade derivation (trade-math)
- Gross P&L is signed price difference times Quantity times multiplier: Long uses exit minus entry, Short inverts it.
- Net P&L is Gross P&L minus Fees.
- Default Risked Amount is absolute entry-to-stop distance times Quantity times multiplier; it is 0 when no stop price is set.
- An explicit Risked Amount override replaces the default; derived Gross/Net never change because of it.
- R-Multiple is Net P&L divided by Risked Amount, and is 0 when nothing was risked (never NaN or Infinity).
- A Trade is a Win when Net P&L is above 0, a Loss when below 0, Breakeven when exactly 0.
- An empty chart URL is valid; a non-empty one must be http(s), so ftp and javascript schemes are rejected.
- Tags are optional free-form labels per Trade; derivation trims them, drops blanks, dedupes exact-case, preserves casing, and defaults pre-tag Trades to empty.
- Playbook rules are optional plain-text conditions per Setup, at most ten; rule hygiene trims, drops blanks, dedupes exact-case, preserves casing.
- A Trade stores a frozen snapshot of `{rule text, followed}` pairs as shown at log time; later Setup rule edits never move old snapshots.
- Compliance is followed over total snapshot rules times 100 when the checklist was touched; untouched or rule-less Trades are unscored (null, never 0); all-skipped reads 0, all-followed reads 100.
- Readers normalize legacy Trades missing rules or Compliance to unscored with an empty snapshot.

## Dashboard derivation (computeMetrics, the single shared seam)
- Total Trades counts every logged Trade.
- Win Rate is Wins divided by Wins plus Losses times 100; Breakeven never moves it and an empty journal reads 0.
- Net total is the plain sum of Net P&L, so Short, multiplier, and Fees flow through unchanged.
- Average Win and Average Loss are Net means of their buckets; each reads 0 when its bucket is empty.
- Profit Factor is summed Win Net over absolute summed Loss Net; it is Infinity with wins but no losses and 0 with no wins.
- Day Win Rate buckets Net by UTC close day and rates winning days over nonzero days times 100; flat days are excluded, mirroring Win Rate.
- The balance curve anchors at the active Portfolio's starting balance on the first close, then steps close-time-ordered cumulative Net; an empty Portfolio has no curve.
- Max drawdown is the largest peak-to-trough drop over the balance curve including the starting anchor, with pct as drop over peak times 100; empty or never-down reads 0 and 0%, and a zero peak reads 0% (never NaN or Infinity).
- Win/Loss streaks run on close-time-ordered Trades; Breakeven resets both, current is the trailing run (one side always 0), longest is the max run; all read 0 on empty.
- Expectancy is Net total divided by Total Trades with Breakevens included; an empty journal reads 0.
- Recent Trades are newest close first, capped at 10.
- Profit Factor renders as `∞` when infinite, rates render with two decimals.

## Analytics derivation (computeRMetrics + computeBreakdowns, beside the shared seam)
- R-Expectancy is R sum divided by Total Trades with Breakevens and zero-risk 0Rs included; an empty journal reads 0.
- Median R runs over all stored R-Multiples sorted ascending; an even count averages the two middles; empty reads 0.
- R sum is the plain sum of stored R-Multiples; zero-risk Trades contribute 0, never NaN or Infinity.
- Risked total sums Risked Amount and Net total sums Net P&L; risked coverage counts nonzero-risked Trades of Total Trades.
- Breakdown rows group Trades by one dimension (Setup, Asset symbol, Market, Side, Emotion-before, Emotion-after, Mistake, Grade, Tag) with exact case-sensitive match; blank values collapse to a single `(Unspecified)` row.
- A Trade with N Tags counts once under each of its N Tag rows; untagged Trades collapse to `(Unspecified)`; row counts may sum above Total Trades.
- Breakdown rows carry trade count plus Net P&L sum plus Win-rate plus avg R per value, sorted by Net sum descending with alphabetical tiebreak; an empty journal has no rows.
- Breakdown Win-rate is Wins divided by Wins plus Losses times 100 per group with Breakevens excluded; a group with no counted Trades reads 0.
- Breakdown avg R is R sum divided by group size with Breakevens and zero-risk 0Rs included; the tail `Other (n)` row aggregates its raw Trades, never an average of averages.
- Breakdown avg Compliance is Compliance sum over scored Trades only per group with unscored excluded; a group with no scored Trades reads null (rendered as em-dash, never 0%); the tail `Other (n)` row aggregates raw snapshots the same way.
- Compliance correlation splits scored Trades into a 100%-followed bucket versus a partial (<100%) bucket, each carrying trade count plus Net P&L sum plus Win-rate with the shared Win-rate derivation; unscored Trades are counted aside and excluded from both buckets; an empty or fully unscored journal reads zeros.
- Breakdowns cap at the top 20 values by Net order with the remainder in one `Other (n)` row where n counts collapsed values.
- R values render signed with two decimals (`+1.50R`, `-0.75R`, `0.00R`); Net renders signed dollars; Win-rate renders with two decimals plus `%`.
- Time-pattern rows slice Trades by weekday of UTC close (Monday-first), by hour of UTC close (24 fixed `HH:00-HH:59` buckets), and by Hold Duration (`Intraday (<24h)` / `1-3 days` / `Swing (>3d)`); labels display local while bucketing stays UTC like the calendar.
- Hold Duration is `closedAt` minus `openedAt`; exactly 24h reads `1-3 days` and exactly 72h reads `Swing (>3d)`; negative holds read Intraday and no Trade is ever dropped.
- Time-pattern rows render in chronological order (Monday to Sunday, 00 to 23, Intraday to Swing) with all fixed rows present even when empty; each row carries trade count plus Net P&L sum plus Win-rate plus avg R plus avg Compliance with the shared breakdown derivations.
- Time-patterns live on /analytics beside breakdowns and respect the global filter; Journal and Dashboard stay full-journal.

## Store and settings
- Portfolios persist under the `openjournal-portfolios` key as named records carrying an identifier, a display name, and a starting balance; a fresh workspace holds one `default` Portfolio named `Main`; corrupt or empty input falls back to it.
- The active Portfolio (or the read-only All aggregate) persists under `openjournal-active-portfolio` and defaults to All; unknown ids resolve to All.
- Portfolio names are trimmed, blanks are rejected with a named-field message, duplicates are rejected exact-case preserving casing, and the workspace always keeps at least one named Portfolio.
- Trades persist in the `openjournal-trades` SignalDB collection (localStorage) and survive reloads; readers must await readiness first.
- Every Trade carries a Portfolio association; Trades logged while All is active file into the `default` Portfolio, and legacy Trades stored without one read as the Main Portfolio.
- Dashboard, Trades, Journal, Analytics, and Guard evaluation scope to the active Portfolio; All aggregates every Portfolio with its curve anchored at the sum of member starting balances.
- Starting balance is USD-only per Portfolio, defaults to 10000, and persists in its Portfolio record; missing, negative, or corrupt values fall back to default; the legacy single `openjournal-starting-balance` key migrates into the Main record; All shows the summed anchor read-only.
- Trades list newest close first.
- Setup/Emotion/Mistake seeds always offered; user-added values persist under `openjournal-taxonomy`, merge after seeds, and survive reloads; blanks and duplicates are ignored.
- Tag seeds are empty; user Tags grow the list under the `openjournal-taxonomy` `tag` key on log with the same blank/duplicate rules.
- Playbooks persist under the `openjournal-taxonomy` `playbooks` key as `{rules, archived}` per Setup name; legacy taxonomy without that key migrates to rule-less unarchived; archived Setups hide from the log-form Setup picker while their Trades stay in history, breakdowns, and correlation.
- The global filter (close-date range, Asset substring case-insensitive, Setup/Side/Tag exact, Win/Loss/Breakeven/All with Breakevens outside Win and Loss, AND across axes, empty meaning all) is ephemeral session state in the Trades store and resets on reload and on Portfolio switch; it cuts the Trades table, Analytics breakdowns/R-metrics, and a labeled Dashboard strip (count, Net, Win-rate, avg R) while hero, curve, streaks, drawdown, month-Net, and Journal stay full-Portfolio.
- The multiplier defaults by market (Stocks/Crypto/Forex 1, Futures 5, Options 100) on market change and stays editable afterwards.

## Views
- Routes are /dashboard (KPI cards, cumulative chart, recent, filtered-view badge plus strip when filtering), /trades (log form with optional Grade and comma-separated Tags plus the log-form Playbook checklist, full table with Grade, Compliance, and Tags columns plus Grade filter and Needs review C/D preset, global filter bar), /journal (month calendar, day detail, month summary, never filtered), /analytics (R-Expectancy, median, R sum, totals, breakdown by dimension with picker defaulting to Setup and including Tag plus avg Compliance column, Compliance-vs-outcome block with 100%-versus-partial buckets, global filter bar), /settings (one page stacking Portfolios CRUD, Guards editing with the per-active-Portfolio starting balance, Vocabulary, and Playbooks editors); unknown paths redirect to /dashboard.
- The sidebar holds the Portfolio switcher (All plus named books) and a quiet link to /settings; Portfolio create, rename, and confirm-to-delete live only in /settings; every view reads the active Portfolio, and All is read-only (log form locked, and in /settings the Guards and active starting balance are locked with a per-Portfolio explanation, no Guard status).
- Empty states read `No trades yet`, `No recent trades yet`, `No trades this day`.
- Empty submit logs nothing and names each missing field (Asset, positive Quantity/Multiplier, non-negative Fees, both timestamps, valid URL).
- Dates are stored UTC ISO and displayed in local format, never raw ISO.
- Calendar days key off UTC close date; loss days render destructive, gains show a `+` prefix, flat days with Trades show `0` neutral, empty days show no Net.
- Month Net sums the month's Net; month-end balance equals the active starting balance plus cumulative Net through month end, matching Dashboard math.
- Templates use Spartan zinc theme tokens only; no hard-coded palette (enforced by design-tokens.spec.ts).

## Guards (ADR-0003)
- A Guard is an optional daily or weekly brake on Net P&L loss, Trade count, or stop time, distinct from a Playbook Rule; profit targets are out of scope.
- Daily Guards bucket by UTC close date; weekly Guards bucket by full ISO Monday-to-Sunday UTC week even across month edges.
- Loss Guards take a positive USD limit and breach when bucket Net sum is at or below its negation; count Guards count every Trade including Breakevens and breach only above max; stop time is daily-only local HH:MM with breach only on a strictly-after local close.
- Blank or zero unsets a Guard; negative loss/count and malformed stop time are rejected with a named-field message; missing or corrupt stored Guards fall back to unset.
- Guards persist per Portfolio under `openjournal-guards` as daily maxLoss/maxTrades/stopTime plus weekly maxLoss/maxTrades; a legacy single-Portfolio Guard file migrates into the Main book; Guard evaluation always runs on the active Portfolio's Trades and ignores the global filter; All shows no Guard status.
- Guards never block logging; breaches surface as soft warnings only: Journal cells stay neutral when empty, tint green when inside all set Guards and warning plus icon when breached with Net number styling untouched, day detail names breached daily and containing-week Guards, Trades banners today's UTC bucket only, /settings holds the guards editor plus this-week status.
- Guard tints reuse existing semantic success/warning tokens only.
